; On-cycle differential @product (the F23 shape, pinned at the F26 round):
; `t` is a cross-product of deletable data and feeds itself, so the product
; sits inside its own recursive cycle. The `ViewSelfReachable` fence in
; Program::Build's pre-pass rejects this cleanly in all 4 modes ("Cross-
; products over differential (deletable) data inside recursive cycles are
; not yet supported"). F23 recorded an opt-mode EXC_BAD_ACCESS (exit 139)
; inside EliminateDeadFlows' JOIN taint loop on exactly this program; that
; crash no longer reproduces (verified 2026-08-02) and this case fences the
; clean-diagnostic outcome against regression.
#message base(i32 X) @differential.
#message oth(i32 Y) @differential.
#local o(i32 Y).
#local t(i32 X, i32 Y).
#query out(free i32 X, free i32 Y).

o(Y) : oth(Y).
t(X, Y) @product : base(X), o(Y).
t(X, Y) @product : t(X, _A), o(Y).
out(X, Y) : t(X, Y).
